# Enterprise Registry Workspace Layout — Platform Standard

Status: **ENTERPRISE APPROVED** · Sprint foundation: **CO-UX-016**

## Constitutional principles

1. Registry pages are **data-centric** — maximise visible rows.
2. Shared chrome only — `EnterpriseRegistryWorkspaceShell`.
3. Presentation densification must **never** change registry ownership, APIs, permissions, or business logic.
4. Counters are concise: `Contacts (29)` — never shouty uppercase banners.
5. Search / filter toolbar stays sticky; the grid scrolls independently.

## SSOT paths

| Concern | Path |
|---|---|
| Shell | `src/components/catalyst-one/shared/enterprise-registry-workspace-shell.tsx` |
| Tokens / counter helper | `src/constants/enterprise-registry-workspace.ts` |
| Table density | `src/components/catalyst-one/enterprise-grid/enterprise-data-grid.tsx` (`fillViewport`, sticky toolbar) |
| Docs | `docs/co-ux-016/CO-UX-016-REGISTRY-WORKSPACE-OPTIMISATION-REPORT.md` |

## Forbidden

- Page-specific oversized headers that push the table below the fold  
- Parallel registry chrome families  
- Changing filter semantics / query ownership to “save space”

